# Build context exclusions for the `api`/`worker`/`beat` image (Dockerfile) and
# the `gateway` image (gateway/Dockerfile) — both build from the repository root,
# and the api image ends with `COPY . .`, so ANYTHING not excluded here is baked
# into a layer and shipped to every container.
#
# INVARIANT: this file must exclude everything .gitignore treats as secret or as
# local runtime data. The two drifted once and shipped live credentials plus 3013
# tenant vault files inside the image. `unit_tests/test_dockerignore_covers_secrets.py`
# now fails if they drift again — do not remove an entry without updating that test.
#
# Note: `frontend/` builds from its own context (./frontend) using
# frontend/.dockerignore, so excluding it here is safe. `gateway/`, `maintenance/`,
# `ops/` and the root operator scripts (change_password.py, send_email.py, ...) are
# deliberately NOT excluded — they are run inside the container.

# --- Secrets. Never in an image. -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
creds.txt
*.key
*.pem
m.txt

# --- Tenant data and local vault storage -----------------------------------
# `data/` is the bind-mounted vault used by local development, `.tmp_vault/` and
# `.vault_dev/` hold encrypted upload fixtures. None belong in an image.
data/
.tmp_vault/
.vault_dev/

# --- Migration bundles and database dumps (contain .env + the whole vault) ---
kubera-migration-*
*.dump
*.tar.gz
*.sql

# --- Version control and CI -------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Host virtualenv (wrong architecture; the image builds /opt/venv) -------
.venv

# --- Python caches / build artifacts ---------------------------------------
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
dist/
build/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# --- Tests. Not executed inside the image (README runs pytest on the host). --
tests/
unit_tests/
conftest.py
pytest.ini

# --- Frontend: built by frontend/Dockerfile from its own context ------------
frontend/

# --- Celery beat runtime state (lives on the beat_data volume in production) -
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat-schedule.*

# --- Host-side maintenance lock, used by the operator CLI on the host --------
.maintenance.lock

# --- Compose overrides. Dev-only; must never influence a server image -------
docker-compose.override.yml

# --- Large binaries and working documents -----------------------------------
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Editor / OS --------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# --- Agent workspaces --------------------------------------------------------
.superpowers/
.agents/
